### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5090

# Run the requests in order, from top to bottom.
# The data is stored in SQLite and survives restarts, so every "bookedBy" contains {{roomId}}
# (a new room is created on every run). This way R9 (2 bookings per person per day) and
# R7 (overlap) are not affected by the bookings made in a previous run.

### 1. Create room (capacity 10)
# @name createRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 1",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@roomId = {{createRoom.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Get room
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}

### 3. Get a missing room (expected: 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 4. Create booking (expected: 201)
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

###
@bookingId = {{createBooking.response.body.$.id}}

### 5. Get booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### 6. Overlapping booking (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 7. Cancel booking (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### 8. Add your own requests here for the rules in ASSIGNMENT.md

### R1. Empty room name (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "capacity": 10
}

### R1. Capacity 0 (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Room zero",
  "capacity": 0
}

### R2. Missing bookedBy (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R3. End equal to start (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r3-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R4. Attendees 0 (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r4-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 0
}

### R4. Attendees above capacity, 11 > 10 (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r4-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 11
}

### R5. Booking in the past (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r5-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2020-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2020-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R6. Exactly 4 hours (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r6-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R6. 4 hours and 1 minute (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r6-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T13:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T17:01:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R8. Cancel the same booking again (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### R8. Cancel a missing booking (expected: 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/cancel

### R8. The cancelled booking has status "Cancelled" (expected: 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### R8. A cancelled booking frees its interval: same 10:00-12:00 again (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R7. Touching interval, starts exactly at 12:00 when the other ends (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T14:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 404 before validation: missing room + invalid body (expected: 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "",
  "startUtc": "2020-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2020-01-11T09:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 0
}

### Create a large room, capacity 20 (used by R9 and R10)
# @name createBigRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Big room",
  "capacity": 20
}

###
@bigRoomId = {{createBigRoom.response.body.$.id}}

### R9. 1st booking of the day, room 1 (expected: 201)
# @name createR9First
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r9-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T09:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

###
@r9FirstId = {{createR9First.response.body.$.id}}

### R9. 2nd booking of the same day, other room (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{bigRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r9-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R9. 3rd booking of the same day (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r9-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T15:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R9. Same person, the next day (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r9-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-13T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-13T09:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R9. Cancel the 1st booking of the day (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{r9FirstId}}/cancel

### R9. Cancelled bookings do not count: the 3rd booking is accepted now (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r9-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T15:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### R10. Large room (capacity 20), exactly 2 hours (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{bigRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r10-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-14T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-14T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 15
}

### R10. Large room (capacity 20), 2 hours and 1 minute (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{bigRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r10-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-14T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-14T13:01:00Z",
  "attendees": 15
}

### R10. Room with capacity 10 keeps the 4-hour limit: 3 hours (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r10-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-14T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-14T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### R11. Booking that starts in 30 minutes (expected: 201)
# $datetime with an offset is REST Client (VS Code) syntax.
# @name createR11Soon
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r11-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 30 m}}",
  "endUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 90 m}}",
  "attendees": 2
}

###
@r11SoonId = {{createR11Soon.response.body.$.id}}

### R11. Cancel less than 60 minutes before the start (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{r11SoonId}}/cancel

### R11. Booking that starts in 2 hours, in the large room (expected: 201)
# @name createR11Later
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{bigRoomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "r11-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 2 h}}",
  "endUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 3 h}}",
  "attendees": 2
}

###
@r11LaterId = {{createR11Later.response.body.$.id}}

### R11. Cancel more than 60 minutes before the start (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{r11LaterId}}/cancel
